{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-5e6b0c3f5bfdda1004dc","statement":"If $t^\\la\\in \\Gr_{\\leq \\mu}$, then $S_\\la\\cap \\Gr_\\mu$ is non-empty and $S_\\la \\cap \\Gr_{\\leq \\mu}$ is\npure of dimension $(\\rho,\\la+\\mu)$.\n\n- Let $\\mA\\in\\Sat_G$. Then $(q_!i^*\\mA)_\\la=\\on{H}_c^*(S_\\la, \\mA)$ is concentrated in degree $(2\\rho,\\la)$. In addition, there is a canonical isomorphism\n\n$$\\on{H}_c^{(2\\rho,\\la)}(S_\\la, \\IC_\\mu)\\otimes\\Ql((\\rho,\\la+\\mu))\\cong \\Ql[\\on{Irr}(S_\\la\\cap\\Gr_{\\leq \\mu})],$$\n\nwhere the r.h.s is the $\\Ql$-span of irreducible components of $S_\\la\\cap\\Gr_{\\leq \\mu}$.\n\n- There is a canonical isomorphism of functors\n\n$$\\on{H}^*(-)\\cong \\on{CT}:=\\bigoplus_\\la \\on{H}_c^*(S_\\la,-):\\Sat_G\\to \\on{Vect}_{\\Ql}.$$","source_id":"arXiv:1603.05593","cluster":"algebraic_geometry","statement_sha256":"92feb774de279f58e0eda8e813aa8629ff18a5b35fa7c15ff28779fed02b1239","kind":"theorem","label":"Theorem 161","ref_key":"MV theory","name":"","order":193,"deps":[],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.05593","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"9aa0de800bec9f56ae36a0522194f91bc11ab1fe49bff0d4068568a9eb549a68","line":2727,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-27T16:49:20+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v2","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":640,"math_hints":102}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:1603.05593","title":"Guide for Lecturers in the Park City Mathematics Institute","abstract":"We introduce various affine Grassmannians, study their geometric properties, and give some applications. We also discuss the geometric Satake equivalence. These are the expanded lecture notes for a mini-course in 2015 PCMI summer school. References updated and more details added.","authors":["Xinwen Zhu"],"year":"2016","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.05593","cluster":"algebraic_geometr